              ToolMessage(content='I now have a great picture of the London → Paris options. Early June (peak wedding season — long days, mild weather, and gardens in full bloom) is the sweet spot, with plenty of direct easyJet flights at excellent prices. Let me put together my shortlist.\n\nHere\'s my shortlist of the **best one-way London → Paris options for a destination wedding** (economy, early June 2027):\n\n## 💰 Cheapest Options\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|\n| LTN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 06 Jun 06:05 → 08:30 (1h 25m) | Economy | **64 EUR** |\n| LTN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 07 Jun 11:10 → 13:20 (1h 10m) | Economy | **58 EUR** ✨ |\n| LTN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 10 Jun 06:05 → 08:30 (1h 25m) | Economy | 64 EUR |\n| LGW → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 06 Jun 08:10 → 10:30 (1h 20m) | Economy | 66 EUR |\n\n## ⚡ Shortest Options\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 04 Jun 11:20 → 13:30 (**1h 10m**) | Economy | **70 EUR** |\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 07 Jun 11:10 → 13:20 (**1h 10m**) | Economy | **58 EUR** ✨ |\n| SEN → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 03 Jun 10:10 → 12:20 (**1h 10m**) | Economy | 72 EUR |\n| LGW → CDG (easyJet, direct) | 06 Jun 08:10 → 10:30 (1h 20m) | Economy | 66 EUR |\n\n## 🏆 Other Notable Option\n| Route | Times & Duration | Cabin | Price |\n|-------|------------------|-------|-------|\n| LHR → CDG (Air France, direct) | 06 Jun 06:15 → 08:40 (1h 25m) | Economy | 87 EUR |\n\n*Best value from Heathrow if you prefer a full-service airline (Air France, arrives CDG)!* (Cheapest LHR→CDG option was 87 EUR.)\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 Summary & Recommendation\n\n- **Best price:** **58 EUR** — easyJet SEN→CDG, Mon 7 Jun 2027, 11:10 → 13:20 (only 1h 10m). It\'s literally the cheapest *and* tied for shortest. A no-brainer.\n- **Great all-rounder:** **64 EUR** easyJet LTN→CDG on Sun 6 Jun, 06:05 → 08:30 — land early and have the whole day for wedding prep.\n- **If flying from Heathrow matters:** Air France at 87 EUR.\n\n**My pick:** Go with the **easyJet Southend flight at 58 EUR** — it\'s the cheapest flight AND one of the fastest. Early June gives you long golden evenings, mild temperatures, and Paris\'s gardens at their most romantic for the big day. 🥂\n\n*Fun fact: Paris is informally called "la Ville Lumière" — the City of Light — not just for the Eiffel Tower sparkle, but because it was one of the first cities in the world to install street lighting back in the 1800s. Enjoy your destination wedding under those lights!* ✨', name='search_flights', id='6b31833f-468f-419e-9982-87a92e7cb750', tool_call_id='call_804da1706a7c4f6d8f1391dd'),
              ToolMessage(content='Based on my research (12 searches), here are the best wedding venue options in Paris for 100 guests, evaluated on price (lowest), capacity (exact match), and reviews (highest):\n\n## 🏆 Top Recommendations\n\n### 1. La Maison de Charly (Restaurant, Paris)\n- **Capacity:** 100 dining (exact match!) / 150 reception\n- **Price:** €4,000–€6,000 (venue hire)\n- **Reviews:** Rated "Excellent" across ~59 reviews on Trip.com; 6 wedding reviews on Bridebook\n- **Why:** Exact capacity match at a very competitive price. Privatized Mediterranean/Moroccan restaurant with great food/service feedback, dancefloor, and church within walking distance.\n\n### 2. Péniche Le Grand Bleu (Seine River Boat, Paris 15th)\n- **Capacity:** Up to 120 seated / 150 cocktail (fits 100 comfortably)\n- **Price:** €1,750–€4,700 (Bridebook) / from €2,500 (ABC Salles)\n- **Reviews:** Highly praised for weddings ("Dream wedding," superb crew, attentive staff)\n- **Why:** One of the lowest price points, plus a unique floating venue with Paris monument views—great value for 100 guests.\n\n### 3. La Fabrique République (Industrial-chic venue, Paris 10th)\n- **Capacity:** 150 guests (multiple rooms; L\'Atelier seats 100 banquet)\n- **Price:** €3,500–€8,000 (venue hire; from €3,000/day private hire)\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (37 reviews)\n- **Why:** Exceptional 5-star rating, very affordable, exclusive use, flexible spaces, and external catering permitted.\n\n### 4. L\'Olivia (Paris)\n- **Capacity:** 140 guests (fits 100 easily)\n- **Price:** €1,500–€10,000\n- **Reviews:** ⭐ 5.0 (43 reviews)\n- **Why:** Top-rated with a wide price range and low entry point; outdoor space, city view, exclusive use.\n\n---\n\n## 💎 Other Strong Options (Higher Budget)\n\n| Venue | Capacity | Price | Rating |\n|-------|----------|-------|--------|\n| **Maison de l\'Amérique Latine** (7th) | 220 (min 80) | from €260 pp (~€26k) | 3 wedding reviews; gorgeous Saint-Germain gardens |\n| **Hôtel Particulier Montmartre** (18th) | up to 200 | from €11,500 | ⭐ 4.3 (2,776 reviews) |\n| **Chteau de Saint-Martin-du-Tertre** (Île-de-France) | 100 (exact) | from €10,000 | ⭐ 4.9 (78 reviews) |\n\n---\n\n## 📌 Summary\nFor the **best overall balance** (low price + high reviews + exact capacity), I recommend **La Maison de Charly** and **La Fabrique République**. If you want a memorable, lower-cost Seine-side experience, **Péniche Le Grand Bleu** is an outstanding value option. The **palace-style hotels** (Four Seasons George V, Peninsula, Ritz) also accommodate 100 but run €100,000+ all-in, so they fall well outside the value tier.\n\n*Note: Always confirm final quotes directly—Parisian venues often add 20% TVA and catering minimums. Prices above are venue-hire figures unless noted.*', name='search_venues', id='b54401e3-128f-43f9-a45a-ebbdf5c6bde3', tool_call_id='call_64ebdc3ecfd34c9083c1b0fe'),
              ToolMessage(content='I\'ve found a ready-made **"Wedding Jazz"** playlist in the database (PlaylistId 19), packed with romantic standards, bossa nova classics, and smooth jazz — perfect for a wedding. Here\'s the curated playlist:\n\n## 💍 Wedding Jazz Playlist\n\n**Bossa Nova Classics (Romantic, Light)**\n1. Desafinado – 3:05\n2. Garota De Ipanema – 4:45\n3. Samba De Uma Nota Só (One Note Samba) – 2:17\n4. Ligia – 4:12\n5. Fotografia – 2:09\n6. Dindi – 4:13\n7. Falando De Amor – 3:40\n8. Angela – 2:50\n9. Corcovado (Quiet Nights Of Quiet Stars) – 3:26\n10. Outra Vez – 2:07\n11. O Boto (Bôto) – 6:07\n12. Canta, Canta Mais – 4:32\n\n**Timeless Standards (Perfect for First Dance)**\n13. \'Round Midnight – 5:57\n14. Bye Bye Blackbird – 7:56\n15. New Rhumba – 4:38\n16. Summertime – 3:20\n17. So What – 9:24\n18. Someday My Prince Will Come – 9:04\n19. My Funny Valentine (Live) – 15:08\n20. Time After Time – 3:41\n21. How High The Moon – 3:21\n22. Imagination – 4:49\n23. Don\'t Take Your Love From Me – 4:42\n24. I\'m Coming Virginia – 4:40\n\n**Smooth Jazz / Contemporary (Easy Listening for Guests)**\n25. Love Is The Colour – 4:12\n26. Gypsy – 5:31\n27. Sunchild – 4:20\n28. My Ship – 4:28\n29. Miles Ahead – 3:30\n30. Morning Dance – 3:59\n31. Jubilee – 4:35\n32. Song For Lorraine – 4:00\n33. Starburst – 4:52\n34. Heliopolis – 5:39\n35. Amanda – 4:07\n36. Despertar – 5:07\n37. OAM\'s Blues – 4:27\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Playlist Summary\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Number of tracks** | 37 |\n| **Total duration** | **10,729,027 ms ≈ 178.8 minutes (~2 hrs 58 min)** |\n| **Total cost** | **$36.63** (37 tracks × $0.99) |\n\nThis playlist flows beautifully from breezy bossa nova during cocktail hour, into timeless standards for the ceremony and first dance (including legendary Miles Davis tracks), and finishes with smooth contemporary jazz for dinner and late-evening mingling. Total runtime is just under 3 hours — ideal for covering a full wedding celebration. 🎷✨', 